{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Initialises a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantBuilder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" structure."}],"metadata":{"title":"init_(type:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:4GLib22VariantBuilderProtocolPAAE5init_4typeyqd___tAA0b4TypeD0Rd__lF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"init_","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"VariantTypeT","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"type"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VariantTypeT","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"extendedModule":"GLib"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"init_"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"VariantTypeT"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"type","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VariantTypeT","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"VariantTypeT"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VariantTypeProtocol","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib19VariantTypeProtocolP","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantTypeProtocol","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" must be non-","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":".  It specifies the type of container to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"construct.  It can be an indefinite type such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"G_VARIANT_TYPE_ARRAY","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a definite type such as “as” or “(ii)”.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Maybe, array, tuple, dictionary entry and variant-typed values may be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constructed."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If using a static type such as one of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"G_VARIANT_TYPE_*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" constants","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"or a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G_VARIANT_TYPE (\"(ii)\")"},{"type":"text","text":" macro, it is more performant to use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_builder_init_static()"},{"text":" rather than ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_builder_init()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"After the builder is initialised, values are added using","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_builder_add_value()"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_builder_add()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After all the child values are added, "},{"code":"g_variant_builder_end()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" frees","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the memory associated with the builder and returns the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","isActive":true},{"text":" that","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was created."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This function completely ignores the previous contents of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"builder"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"On one hand this means that it is valid to pass in completely"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"uninitialised memory.  On the other hand, this means that if you are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"initialising over top of an existing "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantBuilder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" you need to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_builder_clear()"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to avoid leaking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"memory.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You must not call ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_variant_builder_ref()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_builder_unref()"},{"type":"text","text":" on a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantBuilder","isActive":true},{"text":" that was initialised","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with this function.  If you ever pass a reference to a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantBuilder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" outside of the control of your own code then you","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should assume that the person receiving that reference may try to use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"reference counting; you should use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_builder_new()"},{"text":" instead of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this function."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/variantbuilderprotocol\/init_(type:)"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation